Source: lazyvim-git
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ackerman-00 <noreply@example.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/LazyVim/LazyVim

Package: lazyvim-git
Architecture: all
# Runtime requirements per upstream README: Neovim >= 0.11.2, Git >= 2.19.0
# (mirrors the RPM spec Requires).
Depends: git (>= 2.19.0), neovim (>= 0.11.2), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Neovim setup for lazy people (git snapshot)
 LazyVim is a Neovim setup powered by lazy.nvim to make it easy to
 customize and extend your configuration.
